{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What is a Layout?  "}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the layout."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Interpret the technical design report, to determine the work plan during the phase of building the software, based on regulation ad protocols established by the company. Designs the graphic layout of the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the graphic layout of an IT solution, functional requirements of a business through the IT solution, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future with \"Will\": Interrogative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use&nbsp;<strong>will</strong>&nbsp;to talk about actions that you plan to do in the future.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>To create a statement using&nbsp;<strong>will</strong>, you need to take into account the following information:&nbsp;<br /><br />For&nbsp;<strong>affirmative statements</strong>, you use&nbsp;<strong>will&nbsp;</strong>and a verb in its base form.&nbsp;<br /><br />Structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br />Subject + Will + Verb in base form + Complement</p> <p><br />Example:<br /><i>I&nbsp;<strong>will</strong>&nbsp;design an amazing web page.&nbsp;<br /><br /></i>For&nbsp;<strong>negative statements</strong>, you use&nbsp;<strong>not&nbsp;</strong>after&nbsp;<strong>will</strong>&nbsp;or the contraction&nbsp;<strong>won't</strong>&nbsp;, and the verb in its base form.&nbsp;<br /><br />Structure:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br />Subject + Will + Not + Verb in base form + Complement</p> <p><br />Example:<br /><i>I&nbsp;<strong>will not</strong>&nbsp;use the left alignment in this web page.&nbsp;<br /><br /></i>For&nbsp;<strong>interrogative statements</strong>, you need to place the auxiliary&nbsp;<strong>will&nbsp;</strong>at the beginning of the statement and a question mark \"?\" at the end.&nbsp;<br /><br />If needed, you can include a WH in the beginning of the question to ask for specific information.&nbsp;<br /><br />Structure:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br />WH (optional) +Will+Subject+ Verb in base form + Complement + ?</p> <p><br />Example:<br /><i>How&nbsp;<strong>will</strong>&nbsp;the layout achieve a balance between the flow of information and the eye movement?<br /><strong>Will</strong>&nbsp;the new layout help our clients understand better what we do?</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Will you instruct me?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How will those aspects help the web page improvement?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Will you tell me what it is?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That will help with the legibility and readability."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "design"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make or create something in a technical way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm just checking how the new design for the web page is going to be."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "readability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "characteristic of a text that can be read in a smooth way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So, you might want to take into consideration aspects like legibility, alignment, type size, and readability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "complain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show dissatisfaction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It seems that most of our clients as well as the company staff have been complaining about it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "alignment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way a text is displayed in terms of position"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So, you might want to take into consideration aspects like legibility, alignment, type size, and readability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "improvement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "getting better"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How will those aspects help the web page improvement?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legibility"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "synonym of readability"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's why you ought to have a good type size. That will help with the legibility and readability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find information about design rules. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose the most important rules. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a friso to explain the rules you chose."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share and explain the rules to your partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about design rules."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a friso I write the most important rules. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partner important design rules. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What is a layout?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "All of the items displayed on a web page, advertisement, book or magazine are part of the layout."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The layout is any published or printed work that you may find in a book, magazine, advertisement, or web site. The layout displays the organization of elements like titles, colors, images, etc.&nbsp;<br /><br />It is important to present information in a friendly way for visitors, in the case of web pages, or readers, for magazines, advertisements, and books. That is why you have to keep in mind that the layout's appearance must be organized; giving the appropriate smooth flow of information for readers or visitors.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Layout is all the appearance a web page has. It includes some aspects such as titles, colors, graphics and information presented on the web page."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The idea is that the layout achieves a balance between the flow of information and the customer's eye movement. That's why you ought to have a good type size. That will help with the legibility and readability."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>Hi Stephanie, what are you up to?&nbsp;<br /><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Hi, I'm just checking how the new design for the web page is going to be.<br /><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>New design?<br /><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Yes, the boss told me that we'd better change the web page layout. It seems that most of our clients, as well as the company staff, have been complaining about it.<br /><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>I'm sorry; I don't know what a layout is. Will you tell me what it is?</p>"}, {"time": "21000", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Yes, of course. The layout is the appearance a web page has. It includes some aspects such as titles, colors, graphics, and information presented on the web page.&nbsp;<br /><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>I understand. Why are clients complaining about the web page?&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Well, there are some rules you ought to follow to design a web page. The person in charge of designing the page previously didn't take them into account.&nbsp;</p>\n<br /><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>What are those rules you refer to?<br /><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Let's imagine you are creating a web page. So, you might want to take into consideration aspects like legibility, alignment, and type size.&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "56000", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>How will those aspects help the web page improvement?</p>\n<p><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>The idea is that the layout achieves a balance between the flow of information and the customer's eye movement. That's why you ought to have a good type size. That will help with the legibility and readability. If you want to establish a good communication with the viewer, you need to ask yourself: \"Will customers have issues trying to read the information displayed?\" That information, in this company's case, ought to be left aligned since it is the most common, easiest and most legible way for customers.</p>\n<p><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>Are there any other alignments?&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Yes, there are right, central, and justified alignments.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Thomas:&nbsp;</strong>Will you instruct me?&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Stephanie:&nbsp;</strong>Of course I will.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n5le03ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain what a layout is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe different design rules."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What is the appropriate way to display information on a web page?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are some design techniques you need to take into account when creating a web page?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "This layout is not user friendly!"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id":